{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462325-what-kind-of-art-would-you-like-to-see-in-future-products","id":1462325,"title":"What Kind of Art Would You Like To See In Future Products?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-01T14:42:04-07:00","id":1462325,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What Kind of Art Would You Like To See In Future Products?","content":"There is always talk about the art in any new VtM product. Something that kind of bothers me is that they emphasise the gothic punk and personal horror, but that art has never screamed that to me, at least not in the Anarch and Blood Cult books anyway. Although I am looking forward to the Sabbat book which apparently has pretty good art. But the art in the books I've seen, and even stuff from Bloodhunt and Bloodlines, makes me think of GTA by Night rather than gothic punk personal horror. What are your thoughts on the current art direction of VtM and what style would you like to see in the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T15:43:02-07:00","id":1462332,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more of timebrooks work again. I really liked his sketches in dark ages/revised and the way clan sketches perfectly encompass the clan. In terms of avoidance I didn't really like the photoshoots. Frankly I wouldn't mind more black and whites as well.","signatu